\begin{lemma}\label{lem:main-symmetrizer}
Identify the right spherical module with $C_{W_0}\mathcal H_{\rm aff}$
by $M_e\mapsto C_{W_0}$, where $M_eH_i=v^{-1}M_e$ for $1\le i<N$.
In the inverse-permutation convention,
\begin{gather}\label{eq:marked-symmetrizer}
\mathcal R_m=\frac{M_eC_JC_KC_V}{d_m},\qquad
d_m=h_Vh_L^2=[m]!^2[m-1]!^4.
\end{gather}
This quotient is integral and bar invariant.
\end{lemma}

\begin{remark}
The use of parabolic chains is classical in the Schur algebroid;
see \cite{Williamson}. Elias--Ko relate this combinatorics
to ordinary type~$A$ webs via an associated graded construction
\cite{EliasKo}.
For products of parabolic KL elements and their canonical
corrections, see also \cite{AgrawalSotirov}.
\end{remark}

\begin{lemma}\label{lem:finite-flag-count}
Over $\mathbb F_Q$, the number of galleries is $F_A(Q)$.
\end{lemma}

